# ouroboros#157 (round 117, the boundness bit): `prev of z` where z is bound
# only in a NOT-TAKEN branch. A module numeric is a C static live from
# program start; the VM's binding exists only from its first executed
# assignment. HEAD printed null rc 0 where the VM dies rc 1. The bit
# (`static int eig_z_b`, set at every store) makes the read die like the VM.
q is 1
print of "before"
if q == 5:
    z is 7
print of (prev of z)
print of "unreachable"
